WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:06.680
All living things are made out of cells.
Every cell is surrounded by a thin film

2
00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:10.350
called a membrane, stuffed with the
machinery and instructions for life.

3
00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:15.950
Cells come in a huge variety of shapes
and sizes. Every cell excels at a

4
00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:17.250
particular job.

5
00:00:18.430 --> 00:00:21.960
Different cells have different
structures. Bacteria and plant cells

6
00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:26.880
have a tough wall surrounding them, but
our cells don't. Our cells have smaller

7
00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:30.590
containers inside, called organelles,
while bacteria don't.

8
00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:36.250
Most living things can exist as just a
single cell, like bacteria or amoeba,

9
00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:41.100
but animals and plants are formed from
many cells stuck together. Cells are

10
00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:46.440
often very small. Most bacteria are
100,000 times smaller than a grain of

11
00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:51.670
rice. Some of our cells are much larger.
Our neurons can reach from our heads to

12
00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:52.370
our toes.

13
00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:57.760
Shape is very important for cells.
Neurons allow our brains to tell our

14
00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:02.530
toes how to move, so they are long and
narrow like wires. Bacteria need to

15
00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:05.770
move around, so they have tiny
propellers that allow them to swim.

16
00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:11.040
Trillions of small cells can make a
majestic narwhal, a beating heart, and

17
00:01:11.050 --> 00:01:15.860
a kitten's nose. We start as a single
cell, which splits into two, then four,

18
00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:20.410
then eight and so on, until some cells
specialize to become your gut, your

19
00:01:20.410 --> 00:01:22.690
brain and all other parts of your body.

20
00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:28.890
Some cells can crawl. Some can transmit
electricity. Some cells can eat other

21
00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:34.380
cells. Some cells can capture sunlight.
Some can glow. What other different

22
00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:38.470
types of cells can you think of? How do
their unique shapes and sizes help them

23
00:01:38.470 --> 00:01:40.070
perform their jobs?

